/// The second declarer of the leaf `stash`, so that `stash` is PLURAL.
///
/// Its only job is to push `Main`'s bare `stash(1)` off the binder's
/// single-overload fast path (door 2) and into multi-candidate selection
/// (door 3).  Same signature as `Vault::stash` on purpose: a different one
/// would be filtered out by signature matching before selection ever runs,
/// and the call would take the fast path after all.
///
/// `Main` does NOT import this module, so this candidate classifies as Hidden
/// and `Vault::stash` is the one selected -- which is the point.  It is
/// `public` so that nothing here contributes a second visibility error and
/// muddies which door produced which diagnostic.
///
/// `Vault` imports and calls it. That is not decoration: module discovery is
/// import-driven, so a file nothing imports is never compiled and cannot make
/// any leaf plural. See the note on that import.
namespace VisibilityGate::Annex;

public function stash(v: i32) -> i32 { return v + 100; }
